  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>melarsoprol</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>P01CD01</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>one compartment, IV dosing <small>(PK_1C)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Burri C et al. 1994</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>healthy vervet monkeys</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>melarsoprol</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_melarsoprol/Melarsoprol_Burri1994_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>mean residence time</td><td>18</td><td>h</td><td><small>MRT</small></td></tr><tr><td>volume of distribution</td><td>3.6</td><td>l/kg</td><td><small>V</small></td></tr><tr><td>clearance</td><td>3.5</td><td>ml/min*kg</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr></table><h4>About melarsoprol</h4><p>Melarsoprol is an arsenic-based antiparasitic drug used to treat sleeping sickness (African trypanosomiasis). It has been listed among WHO essential medicines as a trypanocidal agent, but DrugBank currently classifies it as investigational, so its availability today appears limited.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q419753\">Wikidata Q419753</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Melarsoprol\">Melarsoprol</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Burri C et al. (1994). Pharmacokinetics of melarsoprol in uninfected vervet monkeys. <i>Acta tropica 58(1):35–49</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/0001-706x(94)90120-1\">10.1016/0001-706x(94)90120-1</a> PUBMED:<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7863853\">7863853</a></p></li></ol></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Burri_1994: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"),
